Real-World Database Optimization Techniques
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Slow Inventory Search:
If there are many products in different warehouses, finding the stock can take more time.

Suggestion: We can use indexing to make the inventory search faster.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Same Product Ordered by Many Customers
Sometimes two customers may order the same product at the same time. This can create problems with the available stock.

Suggestion: We can use transactions and locking so that the stock is updated correctly.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Large Number of Orders
When the number of orders increases, finding a customer's old orders may take more time.

Suggestion: We can use indexes and show the orders in small pages instead of loading everything at once.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Many Inventory Records
Every sale, return, and stock update creates a new inventory record. After some time, there can be a lot of records.

Suggestion: We can divide the data into smaller parts using partitioning to improve performance.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Reports Take More Time
Sales and inventory reports may take longer when the database has a lot of data.

Suggestion: We can use materialized views for reports that are used frequently, so they can load faster.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
